nk assertion proves the actual canonical symlink target.\n\nThe Quality-workflow test owner uses Bun-hosted Effect Vitest, Effect FileSystem,\nand scoped platform child processes. Its isolated release-boundary suite runs\nall six retained owning commands and six strict-enforcement mutations as\nindependent named tests with their existing five-minute deadlines and scoped\ntemporary repository copies. A separate test proves documentation tools work\nbefore any package build in a fresh source-only copy. The suite preserves\nrelative links and removes each copy on completion or interruption. The native\n      \"tasks\": [\n        \"CSF-T003\",\n        \"CSF-T004\",\n        \"CSF-T005\",\n        \"CSF-T006\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"surface\": \"Version/tooling/lint/skills/CI and exact exports\",\n      \"decision\": \"Change required\",\n      \"paths\": [\n        \"package.json\",\n        \"bun.lock\",\n        \"turbo.json\",\n        \"oxlint.config.ts\",\n        \"oxfmt.config.ts\",\n        \"tsconfig*\",\n        \"knip*.json\",\n        \"tools/oxlint/**\",\n        \"tools/skills/**\",\n        \".agents/skills/**\",\n        \"AGENTS.md\",\n        \".github/workflows/**\",\n        \"tools/quality-workflow/**\"\n      ],\n      \"tasks\": [\n        \"CSF-T002\",\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T001\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"The selected graph is actually installed and built; provisional research is not presented as compatibility proof.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Resolve current official releases, including stable Effect module paths, then qualify one exact Bun/TypeScript/React/Atom/Alchemy/tooling graph in a fresh scratch fixture before integrating it.\",\n        \"Qualify the proposed exact Scheduler peer-metadata correction, or use a newer upstream fix. Preserve valid tax outputs; update package exports/types/imports and versioning consequences deliberately.\",\n        \"Adopt the complete canonical current repository skills (0.6.1 successor of the designed 0.6.0 baseline) and declared TaxKit profiles/receipts, including the required Linear skill folder and Claude link without creating provider projects/issues. Merge all eleven portable strict Effect rules, including no-imperative-collections, and workspace-export direction into the actual lint config across source/tests/tools/config/infrastructure. Reuse baseline mutation/loop/collection checks; add only evidenced gaps and readonly-value checks. Exact Promise-returning/runtime host exceptions do not exempt other constructs.\",\n        \"Extend actual-command positive/negative fixtures under moved paths; assert admitted file counts, exit codes and expected rules. Prove removing/disabling required rules or broadening exact assignment/method exceptions fails the verifier. Refresh Turbo read/input/cache ownership, Knip inventories and CI commands; keep explicit generated/vendor exclusions.\",\n        \"Qualify canonical rejection of let/var, assignments/writes/delete/updates, loops, native array traversal including forEach and mutators/constructors, transient Effect collection modes, switch and manual tag checks. Use existing restrictions and focused corrections for Object/Reflect writes, mutable class/contract values, WeakMap/WeakSet and demonstrated destructured/local aliases. Computed member access is already rejected by no-unchecked-index. Accept persistent collections, pure immutable Effect-managed state and qualified Alchemy Output operations. Preserve/qualify stronger lexical runtime callback/reference checks outside exact hosts. Review helper purpose, Schema ownership and pipe/flat-program call graphs separately; lint alone is not semantic proof.\",\n        \"Cover owned .ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx/.mjs/.cjs files, including retained JavaScript policy tools, in actual lint scope; convert to checked TypeScript where necessary instead of treating the scaffold TypeScript-only override as complete. Executable MDX expressions/imports remai