{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T07:53:10.038Z","ordinal":77912,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac74bdb54c487d090c97d4b003f04e2","status":"completed","call_id":"call_a7f66fb2255d4029b1fb54720ab64c5b","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.mcp__codex_apps__github_create_pull_request({repository_full_name:\"crcorbett/taxkit\",base:\"main\",head:\"codex/merge-all-20261008\",draft:true,title:\"Combine all reviewed TaxKit work and the Medicare correction [skip ci]\",body:\"This combines all 81 open TaxKit PRs into main: the reviewed rebuild and the separately approved 2025–26 Medicare correction (#168). It preserves the plugin migration (#140), Entire settings (#153), original reviewed commits, stable toolchain and all six current journey checks.\\n\\nConflict fixes retire the removed shared-skill checks and fixtures, align current plugin guidance, and preserve the historical checkers' refusal of changed source. One documentation process-test timeout is now a finite 15 seconds; its result assertions are unchanged.\\n\\nValidation is running locally on Cooper's Mac. The earlier combined candidate passed full repository verification, all 34 isolated workflow cases and all 22 built Website/API cases, then exposed two obsolete skill-folder test paths. Those paths are corrected; all 661 active code-rule cases, lint, formatting, docs and runbooks pass. The complete nine-part report for current source `44a5e236460a74285c3894195184a7865371e92b` must pass before merge. [Preparation, failed attempts and recovery](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/44a5e236460a74285c3894195184a7865371e92b/docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-08-merge-all.json).\\n\\nPostHog and metrics stay postponed, collection stays off, and full rebuild acceptance remains open. This repository merge applies no package versions, publishes no packages and makes no new deployment, credential, billing, provider or adad change. Recovery is a reviewed revert of the actual main merge commit to its first parent.\\n\\nAuthority: Cooper's direct instruction on 8 October 2026: “Merge everything”. Merge commits preserve the reviewed identities; `[skip ci]` follows Cooper's instruction to run checks locally while Actions credits are exhausted.\"});\nstore(\"merge-integration-pr\",r);text(r);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a11a78-0d20-79f1-98ee-3fa84f9694e8","create_time":1791445979.3370526}}}
