{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T07:57:07.305Z","ordinal":77995,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a11a78-0d20-79f1-98ee-3fa84f9694e8","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f2d41395-ef51-4b1a-b625-4adf24102393","process_id":"23397","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba /Users/cooper/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '5416,5418p;5440,5446p;5460,5464p'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba /Users/cooper/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '5416,5418p;5440,5446p;5460,5464p'","name":"MEMORY.md","path":"/Users/cooper/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"  5416\t# Task Group: TaxKit release train and Cloudflare/Alchemy docs deployment\n  5417\tscope: repository-local Changesets/versioning and evidence-gated docs deployment automation.\n  5418\tapplies_to: cwd=/Users/cooper/Projects/taxkit and /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/*/taxkit; reuse_rule=release, PR, SHA, and provider state are time-sensitive; inspect current checkout before acting.\n  5440\t## User preferences\n  5441\t\n  5442\t- durable TaxKit artifacts must not expose reference repositories or their checkout paths; use them only as private comparative evidence. [Task 1]\n  5443\t- when the user says “just going to version / changeset for our repo” -> distinguish local Changeset/versioning from npm authentication, tagging, and publication; do not infer publishing authority. [Task 1]\n  5444\t- when the request says “propose improvements only” and “Do not edit, commit, push, deploy or create a SPEC yet” -> stop at recommendations; later implementation in the same rollout was a boundary violation, not precedent. [Task 3]\n  5445\t- when the user asks to “spin up a subthread” for Alchemy code smells/incorrect structure -> keep the audit separate and report-only; compare primary docs and a pinned clone without mutating the main checkout. [Task 4]\n  5446\t- for current infrastructure work, use small coherent slices, keep SPEC/task ledger/active plan synchronized, use plain Australian English and secret-negative receipts, and separate local, hosted, provider and public proof. [Task 6]\n  5460\t- Symptom: lifecycle docs checks report missing frontmatter after moving an active plan to completed. Fix: stage the rename before rerunning checks. If GitHub status initially says no checks, re-read the PR status rollup after trigger propagation. [Task 1]\n  5461\t- Symptom: exact-name GitHub environment GET can recreate a missing environment. Fix: verify deletion through the non-creating repository environment list. [Task 3]\n  5462\t- Symptom: audit notes or proposed patches include `Projects/**` or absolute checkout paths. Fix: keep durable TaxKit documentation portable. Do not edit, commit, push, change credentials, mutate Cloudflare/Alchemy state, or deploy during the report-only audit. [Task 4]\n  5463\t- Symptom: fresh worktree checks fail because `turbo` is absent, or a generic validator rejects `ALC-AUD-*`. Fix: first run `bun install --frozen-lockfile`; use exact local cross-reference assertions and record the validator namespace limitation rather than claiming generic coverage. [Task 4]\n  5464\t- Symptom: `bun run check:doppler-custody` reports `FAIL [doppler-custody] reason=scoped-token`. Fix: obtain a checkout-scoped personal Doppler login and named authority; do not bootstrap, plan against providers, deploy, tear down, merge, or infer hosted proof merely because credentials are discoverable. [Task 6]\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"  5416\t# Task Group: TaxKit release train and Cloudflare/Alchemy docs deployment\n  5417\tscope: repository-local Changesets/versioning and evidence-gated docs deployment automation.\n  5418\tapplies_to: cwd=/Users/cooper/Projects/taxkit and /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/*/taxkit; reuse_rule=release, PR, SHA, and provider state are time-sensitive; inspect current checkout before acting.\n  5440\t## User preferences\n  5441\t\n  5442\t- durable TaxKit artifacts must not expose reference repositories or their checkout paths; use them only as private comparative evidence. [Task 1]\n  5443\t- when the user says “just going to version / changeset for our repo” -> distinguish local Changeset/versioning from npm authentication, tagging, and publication; do not infer publishing authority. [Task 1]\n  5444\t- when the request says “propose improvements only” and “Do not edit, commit, push, deploy or create a SPEC yet” -> stop at recommendations; later implementation in the same rollout was a boundary violation, not precedent. [Task 3]\n  5445\t- when the user asks to “spin up a subthread” for Alchemy code smells/incorrect structure -> keep the audit separate and report-only; compare primary docs and a pinned clone without mutating the main checkout. [Task 4]\n  5446\t- for current infrastructure work, use small coherent slices, keep SPEC/task ledger/active plan synchronized, use plain Australian English and secret-negative receipts, and separate local, hosted, provider and public proof. [Task 6]\n  5460\t- Symptom: lifecycle docs checks report missing frontmatter after moving an active plan to completed. Fix: stage the rename before rerunning checks. If GitHub status initially says no checks, re-read the PR status rollup after trigger propagation. [Task 1]\n  5461\t- Symptom: exact-name GitHub environment GET can recreate a missing environment. Fix: verify deletion through the non-creating repository environment list. [Task 3]\n  5462\t- Symptom: audit notes or proposed patches include `Projects/**` or absolute checkout paths. Fix: keep durable TaxKit documentation portable. Do not edit, commit, push, change credentials, mutate Cloudflare/Alchemy state, or deploy during the report-only audit. [Task 4]\n  5463\t- Symptom: fresh worktree checks fail because `turbo` is absent, or a generic validator rejects `ALC-AUD-*`. Fix: first run `bun install --frozen-lockfile`; use exact local cross-reference assertions and record the validator namespace limitation rather than claiming generic coverage. [Task 4]\n  5464\t- Symptom: `bun run check:doppler-custody` reports `FAIL [doppler-custody] reason=scoped-token`. Fix: obtain a checkout-scoped personal Doppler login and named authority; do not bootstrap, plan against providers, deploy, tear down, merge, or infer hosted proof merely because credentials are discoverable. [Task 6]\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":9083},"formatted_output":"  5416\t# Task Group: TaxKit release train and Cloudflare/Alchemy docs deployment\n  5417\tscope: repository-local Changesets/versioning and evidence-gated docs deployment automation.\n  5418\tapplies_to: cwd=/Users/cooper/Projects/taxkit and /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/*/taxkit; reuse_rule=release, PR, SHA, and provider state are time-sensitive; inspect current checkout before acting.\n  5440\t## User preferences\n  5441\t\n  5442\t- durable TaxKit artifacts must not expose reference repositories or their checkout paths; use them only as private comparative evidence. [Task 1]\n  5443\t- when the user says “just going to version / changeset for our repo” -> distinguish local Changeset/versioning from npm authentication, tagging, and publication; do not infer publishing authority. [Task 1]\n  5444\t- when the request says “propose improvements only” and “Do not edit, commit, push, deploy or create a SPEC yet” -> stop at recommendations; later implementation in the same rollout was a boundary violation, not precedent. [Task 3]\n  5445\t- when the user asks to “spin up a subthread” for Alchemy code smells/incorrect structure -> keep the audit separate and report-only; compare primary docs and a pinned clone without mutating the main checkout. [Task 4]\n  5446\t- for current infrastructure work, use small coherent slices, keep SPEC/task ledger/active plan synchronized, use plain Australian Eng