{"timestamp":"2026-10-08T08:08:55.329Z","ordinal":78165,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac74f84bc6887d093c9b880db4afeff","status":"completed","call_id":"call_e3b0b8105bf64442a4b583cfc8d5cdd4","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:13420,chars:\"\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":2000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport subprocess,json\\nhead=subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD']).decode().strip()\\nbody=f'''This merges all 81 existing open TaxKit PRs into main: the reviewed rebuild and the separately approved 2025–26 Medicare correction (#168). It preserves the already merged plugin migration (#140), Entire setting (#153), all reviewed commits, the stable toolchain and all six current journey checks.\\n\\nThe combined source resolves the removed copied-skill checks and fixtures, aligns current plugin guidance and retains the historical checkers' refusal of changed source. The documentation process tests keep all result assertions with a finite 15-second time limit.\\n\\nAll nine local release checks passed on Cooper's Mac in 1,080.48 seconds at source `44a5e236460a74285c3894195184a7865371e92b`. The SDK package and downstream checks were fresh executions; both built Website/API runs passed all 22 cases, and all 34 isolated workflow cases passed. All 18 selected log hashes and all 1,712 frozen source identities matched. The final follow-up at `{head}` changes only the receipt and plan note; six focused metadata checks pass, and the other 1,711 frozen source files remain unchanged. [Exact qualification, failed attempts, recovery and limits](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/{head}/docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-08-merge-all.json).\\n\\nPostHog and metrics remain postponed, collection remains off, and full rebuild acceptance remains open. This merge applies no package versio